  "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nHello! I set up Homarr yesterday using Docker Compose through DockGE in an Ubuntu 24.04 VM. It works really well (thanks for all your work!), but today I set a custom background image and noticed that it either does not appear at all, leaving behind a white background, or that it gets cut off, again with white background where it gets cut. This is consistently reproducible using Firefox on Linux. See the screenshot below for an example.\n\n<img width=\"2496\" height=\"1236\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/80887019-6465-4eae-9527-4b0c0753948b\" />\n\nFirefox's console says \"Image corrupt or truncated\". No other information is given.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Set a background image\n- Open the dashboard\n\n### Impact\n\nMinor\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_\n\n### Version\n\n1.67.0\n\n### Installation method\n\nDocker Compose\n\n### Browser\n\nFirefox",
